course: dictionary
lesson: 10555
title: Unbox and the unboxing video
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To unbox something means to take it out of its box or packaging. You can unbox a new phone, a toy or a game. The word has «un-» at the start, which often means taking something away or undoing it, like unwrap or unlock.
explain: An unboxing is a video of someone opening a new product and showing it to viewers. Lots of people watch these videos online, and you may have seen them about toys and gadgets.
explain: Many unboxing videos look like a friend sharing, but «many videos of kids unboxing heaps of toys are really adverts». The toys were often given free so that you would want them. Look for words like «ad» or «sponsored» to spot an advert.
explain: Unboxing has a second meaning in computing: it means taking a value out of its wrapper in a program. The idea is the same as before, getting something out of its packaging.
fact: «Unbox» means to take something out of its box or packaging.
fact: An «unboxing» is a video of someone opening a new product and showing it.
fact: Many unboxing videos are paid adverts, even when they look like a friend sharing.
fact: Look for «ad» or «sponsored» to spot an advert.
fact: Comparing yourself with the people in these videos can make you unhappy for no reason.
exercise: «Many videos of kids unboxing heaps of toys are really adverts.» What does unboxing mean in this sentence? | Packing the toys away for the night | *Taking the toys out of their boxes and showing them | Buying toys in a shop | Breaking the toys to see what is inside
exercise: Your friend says, «Watch my unboxing of the new game!» What will the video show? | A teacher unpacking school bags | A film about a famous boxer | *Someone opening a new game and showing it | A cooking show for dinner
exercise: Which words help you spot an advert in an unboxing video? | *Ad or sponsored | Long or short | Blue or red | Happy or fun
test: Why are many unboxing videos adverts? | Because the toys were made in a box | Because the video is always very long | Because the people in them are famous actors | *Because the toys were given free so that you would want them
test: Ella says, «I'm going to unbox my new phone tonight.» What is she going to do? | Post a phone in the post | *Take the new phone out of its packaging | Lose her phone | Turn the phone off for a rest
exam: What does unbox mean? | *To take something out of its box or packaging | To buy a box of toys | To put something back in a box | To break a box into pieces
